From a5663ab358c2c1a2c6559db4f6531574fc1e55e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:05:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/28] test: declare how a test's nodes are connected with
 `topology`

setup_network() connects the nodes as the `topology` class attribute
says:
- "chain": node i+1 connects to node i, then all sync (the previous
  behaviour, still the default);
- "none": no connections;
- explicit (from, to) pairs: those connections, then all sync.

An unknown topology raises ValueError. Overriding setup_network()
remains for setups that topology cannot express.

The 11 tests that overrode setup_network() only to start the nodes
without connecting them now set topology = "none", keeping their
comments. wallet_backup.py sets its four connections as pairs.

A unit test covers each topology. The full functional suite gives the
same per-test results as before.
